    description: "FOUND 2026-10-13 while fixing INV-tazur (PR #1567); NOT reproduced. smart-test splits deleted TEST paths off the selection now, but deleted SOURCE paths still flow into CHANGED_FILE_LIST (the reverse-slice seed) and CHANGED_SOURCE_FILES. The slice runs on the post-change tree, so a deleted module contributes no symbols, and tests that imported it are selected only if they were edited too, or by per_package_fallback's one-test-per-package floor. A change that deletes a module and forgets a test still importing it would then pass the targeted run and fail at full-suite time. Also: a change whose only source edit is a deletion reaches the \"no test files in slice result\" branch and falls back to a full-suite manifest. Question to answer first: does the slice (or the stable hypergumbo) resolve the dangling import edge from the surviving test to the deleted module? If yes, this is a non-issue; record the evidence. If no, seed the selection for deleted sources from the baseline tree (e.g. grep the post-change tests for the deleted module's import path)."  # 0815
